{
  "corpus": "cratefield-tables row validation",
  "version": 1,
  "about": [
    "Triples of (table, input, expected verdict). The Rust validator runs over every",
    "case in crates/tables/tests/corpus.rs. A second implementation in another language",
    "runs over the same file, which is what stops it and the Rust validator disagreeing",
    "about empty versus absent, number coercion, null versus missing, Unicode length and",
    "whitespace.",
    "",
    "How to read it. `tables` is the same shape as the manifest's [tables] section, keyed",
    "by table name. Each case names one of those tables, supplies an `input`, and expects",
    "either {\"verdict\": \"accept\"} or {\"verdict\": \"reject\", \"errors\": [...]}.",
    "",
    "How to run it. Match on `code`, never on a message: codes are the stable vocabulary",
    "and messages are prose that may be reworded. Expected errors are ordered: declared",
    "fields in declaration order, then unknown keys sorted by name. `field` is an empty",
    "string when the row itself is wrong, which is the RFC 6901 pointer to the whole",
    "document.",
    "",
    "The rules a reimplementation has to match, in one place:",
    "1. A row is a JSON object. Anything else is one not_an_object error.",
    "2. null is absence. {\"x\": null} and {} always reach the same verdict.",
    "3. A field must be present only when it is required and has no default.",
    "4. An unknown key is an error, never a dropped key.",
    "5. No coercion. \"42\" is not an integer, 1 is not true, \"true\" is not a boolean.",
    "6. An integer is a JSON number with no fractional part: Number.isInteger(v). 42.0",
    "   is accepted because JSON cannot tell it from 42.",
    "7. Length is Unicode scalar values. In JavaScript that is [...s].length, never",
    "   s.length. No normalisation: e + combining acute is two characters.",
    "8. Nothing is trimmed. Whitespace is part of the value and counts toward length.",
    "9. Bounds are inclusive at both ends.",
    "10. Uniqueness and foreign keys are not checked here. They read other rows."
  ],
  "codes": [
    "not_an_object",
    "unknown_field",
    "required",
    "wrong_type",
    "too_short",
    "too_long",
    "too_small",
    "too_large",
    "not_in_enum",
    "bad_format"
  ],
  "tables": {
    "post": {
      "primary_key": "id",
      "fields": [
        { "name": "id", "kind": "uuid", "required": true },
        { "name": "title", "kind": "text", "required": true },
        { "name": "note", "kind": "text" },
        { "name": "status", "kind": "enum", "values": ["draft", "published"], "required": true, "default": "draft" }
      ]
    },
    "bounded": {
      "primary_key": "id",
      "fields": [
        { "name": "id", "kind": "text" },
        { "name": "short", "kind": "text", "min_len": 1, "max_len": 3 },
        { "name": "count", "kind": "integer", "min": 0, "max": 10 },
        { "name": "ratio", "kind": "real", "min": 0.0, "max": 1.0 }
      ]
    },
    "typed": {
      "primary_key": "id",
      "fields": [
        { "name": "id", "kind": "text" },
        { "name": "count", "kind": "integer" },
        { "name": "ratio", "kind": "real" },
        { "name": "live", "kind": "boolean" },
        { "name": "seen_at", "kind": "timestamp" },
        { "name": "external_id", "kind": "uuid" },
        { "name": "payload", "kind": "json" },
        { "name": "email", "kind": "text", "format": "email" },
        { "name": "site", "kind": "text", "format": "url" }
      ]
    },
    "single": {
      "primary_key": "id",
      "fields": [{ "name": "id", "kind": "text", "required": true }]
    }
  },
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "a complete row is accepted",
      "table": "post",
      "input": {
        "id": "0b3f2d0e-1a4b-4c8d-9e2f-5a6b7c8d9e0f",
        "title": "Hello",
        "note": "a note",
        "status": "published"
      },
      "expect": { "verdict": "accept" }
    },

    {
      "name": "empty string: an empty string is a value, not an absence",
      "why": "The first drift risk. An empty title is present, so `required` is satisfied.",
      "table": "post",
      "input": { "id": "0b3f2d0e-1a4b-4c8d-9e2f-5a6b7c8d9e0f", "title": "" },
      "expect": { "verdict": "accept" }
    },
    {
      "name": "empty string: an absent required field is missing",
      "table": "post",
      "input": { "id": "0b3f2d0e-1a4b-4c8d-9e2f-5a6b7c8d9e0f" },
      "expect": { "verdict": "reject", "errors": [{ "field": "title", "code": "required" }] }
    },
    {
      "name": "empty string: an empty string fails a min_len of 1",
      "table": "bounded",
      "input": { "id": "x", "short": "" },
      "expect": { "verdict": "reject", "errors": [{ "field": "short", "code": "too_short" }] }
    },

    {
      "name": "coercion: a number arriving as a string is rejected",
      "why": "The second drift risk. No coercion, ever.",
      "table": "typed",
      "input": { "id": "x", "count": "42" },
      "expect": { "verdict": "reject", "errors": [{ "field": "count", "code": "wrong_type" }] }
    },
    {
      "name": "coercion: a plain integer is accepted",
      "table": "typed",
      "input": { "id": "x", "count": 42 },
      "expect": { "verdict": "accept" }
    },
    {
      "name": "coercion: an integer written with a decimal point is accepted",
      "why": "JSON has one number type: 42.0 and 42 are the same value. Number.isInteger(42.0) is true.",
      "table": "typed",
      "input": { "id": "x", "count": 42.0 },
      "expect": { "verdict": "accept" }
    },
    {
      "name": "coercion: a fractional number is not an integer",
      "table": "typed",
      "input": { "id": "x", "count": 42.5 },
      "expect": { "verdict": "reject", "errors": [{ "field": "count", "code": "wrong_type" }] }
    },
    {
      "name": "coercion: an integer is an acceptable real",
      "table": "typed",
      "input": { "id": "x", "ratio": 2 },
      "expect": { "verdict": "accept" }
    },
    {
      "name": "coercion: 1 is not true",
      "table": "typed",
      "input": { "id": "x", "live": 1 },
      "expect": { "verdict": "reject", "errors": [{ "field": "live", "code": "wrong_type" }] }
    },
    {
      "name": "coercion: the string \"true\" is not true",
      "table": "typed",
      "input": { "id": "x", "live": "true" },
      "expect": { "verdict": "reject", "errors": [{ "field": "live", "code": "wrong_type" }] }
    },
    {
      "name": "coercion: a boolean is accepted",
      "table": "typed",
      "input": { "id": "x", "live": false },
      "expect": { "verdict": "accept" }
    },

    {
      "name": "null: an explicit null on an optional field is the same as leaving it out",
      "why": "The third drift risk. These two cases must always match each other.",
      "table": "post",
      "input": { "id": "0b3f2d0e-1a4b-4c8d-9e2f-5a6b7c8d9e0f", "title": "Hello", "note": null },
      "expect": { "verdict": "accept" }
    },
    {
      "name": "null: leaving an optional field out is the same as an explicit null",
      "table": "post",
      "input": { "id": "0b3f2d0e-1a4b-4c8d-9e2f-5a6b7c8d9e0f", "title": "Hello" },
      "expect": { "verdict": "accept" }
    },
    {
      "name": "null: an explicit null on a required field is missing",
      "table": "post",
      "input": { "id": "0b3f2d0e-1a4b-4c8d-9e2f-5a6b7c8d9e0f", "title": null },
      "expect": { "verdict": "reject", "errors": [{ "field": "title", "code": "required" }] }
    },
    {
      "name": "null: a required field with a default may be null",
      "why": "`status` is required and defaults to 'draft', so the database supplies it.",
      "table": "post",
      "input": { "id": "0b3f2d0e-1a4b-4c8d-9e2f-5a6b7c8d9e0f", "title": "Hello", "status": null },
      "expect": { "verdict": "accept" }
    },
    {
      "name": "null: a required field with a default may be left out",
      "table": "post",
      "input": { "id": "0b3f2d0e-1a4b-4c8d-9e2f-5a6b7c8d9e0f", "title": "Hello" },
      "expect": { "verdict": "accept" }
    },
    {
      "name": "null: a null json field is an absence, not a JSON null value",
      "table": "typed",
      "input": { "id": "x", "payload": null },
      "expect": { "verdict": "accept" }
    },

    {
      "name": "unicode: an astral emoji is one character, not two and not four",
      "why": "The fourth drift risk. In JavaScript this is [...s].length, never s.length.",
      "table": "bounded",
      "input": { "id": "x", "short": "😀" },
      "expect": { "verdict": "accept" }
    },
    {
      "name": "unicode: four astral emoji are four characters and exceed a max_len of 3",
      "table": "bounded",
      "input": { "id": "x", "short": "😀😀😀😀" },
      "expect": { "verdict": "reject", "errors": [{ "field": "short", "code": "too_long" }] }
    },
    {
      "name": "unicode: a three-character string of four-byte characters fits a max_len of 3",
      "why": "Twelve bytes. A byte count would reject this.",
      "table": "bounded",
      "input": { "id": "x", "short": "😀😀😀" },
      "expect": { "verdict": "accept" }
    },
    {
      "name": "unicode: three precomposed accented characters fit a max_len of 3",
      "table": "bounded",
      "input": { "id": "x", "short": "\u00e9\u00e9\u00e9" },
      "expect": { "verdict": "accept" }
    },
    {
      "name": "unicode: the same three glyphs decomposed are six characters and do not fit",
      "why": "No normalisation. e plus a combining acute renders as one glyph and counts as two. This case and the one above render identically on screen and reach opposite verdicts, which is the point.",
      "table": "bounded",
      "input": { "id": "x", "short": "e\u0301e\u0301e\u0301" },
      "expect": { "verdict": "reject", "errors": [{ "field": "short", "code": "too_long" }] }
    },

    {
      "name": "whitespace: surrounding whitespace counts toward length",
      "why": "The fifth drift risk. Nothing is trimmed: ' ab ' is four characters.",
      "table": "bounded",
      "input": { "id": "x", "short": " ab " },
      "expect": { "verdict": "reject", "errors": [{ "field": "short", "code": "too_long" }] }
    },
    {
      "name": "whitespace: a single space satisfies a min_len of 1",
      "table": "bounded",
      "input": { "id": "x", "short": " " },
      "expect": { "verdict": "accept" }
    },
    {
      "name": "whitespace: a whitespace-only string is present",
      "table": "post",
      "input": { "id": "0b3f2d0e-1a4b-4c8d-9e2f-5a6b7c8d9e0f", "title": "   " },
      "expect": { "verdict": "accept" }
    },
    {
      "name": "whitespace: a leading space breaks an email",
      "table": "typed",
      "input": { "id": "x", "email": " nick@example.com" },
      "expect": { "verdict": "reject", "errors": [{ "field": "email", "code": "bad_format" }] }
    },
    {
      "name": "whitespace: an email with no surrounding space is accepted",
      "table": "typed",
      "input": { "id": "x", "email": "nick@example.com" },
      "expect": { "verdict": "accept" }
    },

    {
      "name": "row: an array is not a row",
      "table": "post",
      "input": [],
      "expect": { "verdict": "reject", "errors": [{ "field": "", "code": "not_an_object" }] }
    },
    {
      "name": "row: a string is not a row",
      "table": "post",
      "input": "id=1",
      "expect": { "verdict": "reject", "errors": [{ "field": "", "code": "not_an_object" }] }
    },
    {
      "name": "row: a null is not a row",
      "table": "post",
      "input": null,
      "expect": { "verdict": "reject", "errors": [{ "field": "", "code": "not_an_object" }] }
    },

    {
      "name": "unknown: a misspelled column is an error, not a dropped key",
      "table": "single",
      "input": { "id": "x", "titel": "Hello" },
      "expect": { "verdict": "reject", "errors": [{ "field": "titel", "code": "unknown_field" }] }
    },
    {
      "name": "unknown: unknown keys come after declared fields and are sorted",
      "table": "single",
      "input": { "zzz": 1, "aaa": 2 },
      "expect": {
        "verdict": "reject",
        "errors": [
          { "field": "id", "code": "required" },
          { "field": "aaa", "code": "unknown_field" },
          { "field": "zzz", "code": "unknown_field" }
        ]
      }
    },

    {
      "name": "enum: a declared value is accepted",
      "table": "post",
      "input": { "id": "0b3f2d0e-1a4b-4c8d-9e2f-5a6b7c8d9e0f", "title": "Hello", "status": "draft" },
      "expect": { "verdict": "accept" }
    },
    {
      "name": "enum: an undeclared value is rejected",
      "table": "post",
      "input": { "id": "0b3f2d0e-1a4b-4c8d-9e2f-5a6b7c8d9e0f", "title": "Hello", "status": "archived" },
      "expect": { "verdict": "reject", "errors": [{ "field": "status", "code": "not_in_enum" }] }
    },
    {
      "name": "enum: matching is case sensitive",
      "table": "post",
      "input": { "id": "0b3f2d0e-1a4b-4c8d-9e2f-5a6b7c8d9e0f", "title": "Hello", "status": "Draft" },
      "expect": { "verdict": "reject", "errors": [{ "field": "status", "code": "not_in_enum" }] }
    },
    {
      "name": "enum: a number is not one of the values",
      "table": "post",
      "input": { "id": "0b3f2d0e-1a4b-4c8d-9e2f-5a6b7c8d9e0f", "title": "Hello", "status": 0 },
      "expect": { "verdict": "reject", "errors": [{ "field": "status", "code": "wrong_type" }] }
    },

    {
      "name": "bounds: an integer at the minimum is inclusive",
      "table": "bounded",
      "input": { "id": "x", "count": 0 },
      "expect": { "verdict": "accept" }
    },
    {
      "name": "bounds: an integer at the maximum is inclusive",
      "table": "bounded",
      "input": { "id": "x", "count": 10 },
      "expect": { "verdict": "accept" }
    },
    {
      "name": "bounds: an integer below the minimum is rejected",
      "table": "bounded",
      "input": { "id": "x", "count": -1 },
      "expect": { "verdict": "reject", "errors": [{ "field": "count", "code": "too_small" }] }
    },
    {
      "name": "bounds: an integer above the maximum is rejected",
      "table": "bounded",
      "input": { "id": "x", "count": 11 },
      "expect": { "verdict": "reject", "errors": [{ "field": "count", "code": "too_large" }] }
    },
    {
      "name": "bounds: a real below the minimum is rejected",
      "table": "bounded",
      "input": { "id": "x", "ratio": -0.0001 },
      "expect": { "verdict": "reject", "errors": [{ "field": "ratio", "code": "too_small" }] }
    },
    {
      "name": "bounds: a real above the maximum is rejected",
      "table": "bounded",
      "input": { "id": "x", "ratio": 1.0001 },
      "expect": { "verdict": "reject", "errors": [{ "field": "ratio", "code": "too_large" }] }
    },
    {
      "name": "bounds: a real at both ends is inclusive",
      "table": "bounded",
      "input": { "id": "x", "ratio": 1.0 },
      "expect": { "verdict": "accept" }
    },

    {
      "name": "timestamp: an RFC 3339 instant in UTC is accepted",
      "table": "typed",
      "input": { "id": "x", "seen_at": "2026-09-08T09:30:00Z" },
      "expect": { "verdict": "accept" }
    },
    {
      "name": "timestamp: a fractional second is accepted",
      "why": "This is what new Date().toISOString() emits.",
      "table": "typed",
      "input": { "id": "x", "seen_at": "2026-09-08T09:30:00.123Z" },
      "expect": { "verdict": "accept" }
    },
    {
      "name": "timestamp: a numeric offset is accepted",
      "table": "typed",
      "input": { "id": "x", "seen_at": "2026-09-08T09:30:00+02:00" },
      "expect": { "verdict": "accept" }
    },
    {
      "name": "timestamp: a space instead of T is rejected",
      "table": "typed",
      "input": { "id": "x", "seen_at": "2026-09-08 09:30:00Z" },
      "expect": { "verdict": "reject", "errors": [{ "field": "seen_at", "code": "bad_format" }] }
    },
    {
      "name": "timestamp: a lowercase z is rejected",
      "why": "One spelling only. Uppercase T and Z is what toISOString() produces.",
      "table": "typed",
      "input": { "id": "x", "seen_at": "2026-09-08T09:30:00z" },
      "expect": { "verdict": "reject", "errors": [{ "field": "seen_at", "code": "bad_format" }] }
    },
    {
      "name": "timestamp: no offset at all is rejected",
      "table": "typed",
      "input": { "id": "x", "seen_at": "2026-09-08T09:30:00" },
      "expect": { "verdict": "reject", "errors": [{ "field": "seen_at", "code": "bad_format" }] }
    },
    {
      "name": "timestamp: a day the month does not have is rejected",
      "table": "typed",
      "input": { "id": "x", "seen_at": "2026-02-30T09:30:00Z" },
      "expect": { "verdict": "reject", "errors": [{ "field": "seen_at", "code": "bad_format" }] }
    },
    {
      "name": "timestamp: 29 February in a leap year is accepted",
      "table": "typed",
      "input": { "id": "x", "seen_at": "2024-02-29T09:30:00Z" },
      "expect": { "verdict": "accept" }
    },
    {
      "name": "timestamp: 29 February in a common year is rejected",
      "table": "typed",
      "input": { "id": "x", "seen_at": "2026-02-29T09:30:00Z" },
      "expect": { "verdict": "reject", "errors": [{ "field": "seen_at", "code": "bad_format" }] }
    },
    {
      "name": "timestamp: a date with no time is rejected",
      "table": "typed",
      "input": { "id": "x", "seen_at": "2026-09-08" },
      "expect": { "verdict": "reject", "errors": [{ "field": "seen_at", "code": "bad_format" }] }
    },
    {
      "name": "timestamp: a unix epoch number is not a timestamp",
      "table": "typed",
      "input": { "id": "x", "seen_at": 1757324400 },
      "expect": { "verdict": "reject", "errors": [{ "field": "seen_at", "code": "wrong_type" }] }
    },

    {
      "name": "uuid: a lowercase hyphenated UUID is accepted",
      "table": "typed",
      "input": { "id": "x", "external_id": "0b3f2d0e-1a4b-4c8d-9e2f-5a6b7c8d9e0f" },
      "expect": { "verdict": "accept" }
    },
    {
      "name": "uuid: an uppercase UUID is accepted",
      "table": "typed",
      "input": { "id": "x", "external_id": "0B3F2D0E-1A4B-4C8D-9E2F-5A6B7C8D9E0F" },
      "expect": { "verdict": "accept" }
    },
    {
      "name": "uuid: a braced UUID is rejected",
      "table": "typed",
      "input": { "id": "x", "external_id": "{0b3f2d0e-1a4b-4c8d-9e2f-5a6b7c8d9e0f}" },
      "expect": { "verdict": "reject", "errors": [{ "field": "external_id", "code": "bad_format" }] }
    },
    {
      "name": "uuid: an unhyphenated UUID is rejected",
      "table": "typed",
      "input": { "id": "x", "external_id": "0b3f2d0e1a4b4c8d9e2f5a6b7c8d9e0f" },
      "expect": { "verdict": "reject", "errors": [{ "field": "external_id", "code": "bad_format" }] }
    },
    {
      "name": "uuid: a ULID is not a UUID",
      "why": "The harness mints ULIDs. A uuid field is for an identifier that arrives from elsewhere.",
      "table": "typed",
      "input": { "id": "x", "external_id": "01JBQ7X4M8Z9WQ2K3T5V6N7P8R" },
      "expect": { "verdict": "reject", "errors": [{ "field": "external_id", "code": "bad_format" }] }
    },

    {
      "name": "url: an https URL is accepted",
      "table": "typed",
      "input": { "id": "x", "site": "https://factory0.ventures/ventures" },
      "expect": { "verdict": "accept" }
    },
    {
      "name": "url: an http URL is accepted",
      "table": "typed",
      "input": { "id": "x", "site": "http://localhost:8787" },
      "expect": { "verdict": "accept" }
    },
    {
      "name": "url: a scheme other than http or https is rejected",
      "table": "typed",
      "input": { "id": "x", "site": "ftp://example.com" },
      "expect": { "verdict": "reject", "errors": [{ "field": "site", "code": "bad_format" }] }
    },
    {
      "name": "url: a relative path is rejected",
      "table": "typed",
      "input": { "id": "x", "site": "/ventures" },
      "expect": { "verdict": "reject", "errors": [{ "field": "site", "code": "bad_format" }] }
    },
    {
      "name": "url: a space anywhere is rejected",
      "table": "typed",
      "input": { "id": "x", "site": "https://example.com/a b" },
      "expect": { "verdict": "reject", "errors": [{ "field": "site", "code": "bad_format" }] }
    },
    {
      "name": "url: an empty authority is rejected",
      "table": "typed",
      "input": { "id": "x", "site": "https:///ventures" },
      "expect": { "verdict": "reject", "errors": [{ "field": "site", "code": "bad_format" }] }
    },

    {
      "name": "json: an object is accepted",
      "table": "typed",
      "input": { "id": "x", "payload": { "a": 1 } },
      "expect": { "verdict": "accept" }
    },
    {
      "name": "json: an array is accepted",
      "table": "typed",
      "input": { "id": "x", "payload": [1, 2, 3] },
      "expect": { "verdict": "accept" }
    },
    {
      "name": "json: a scalar is accepted",
      "table": "typed",
      "input": { "id": "x", "payload": 7 },
      "expect": { "verdict": "accept" }
    },

    {
      "name": "order: declared fields are reported in declaration order",
      "table": "post",
      "input": { "title": 1, "status": "archived", "extra": true },
      "expect": {
        "verdict": "reject",
